PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The panel maintains a solid and unanimous consensus on **D. Atrial septal defect** (specifically an ostium primum defect). 

The decisive finding is the electrocardiographic pairing of left axis deviation and right ventricular hypertrophy, which is the pathognomonic hallmark of an ostium primum ASD resulting from congenital conduction system displacement combined with right heart volume overload. The systolic ejection murmur, radiation to the clavicle, palpable thrill, and inspiratory augmentation represent a hyperdynamic functional pulmonic flow murmur driven by a large left-to-right shunt. In contrast, isolated pulmonic stenosis (Choice H) causes right axis deviation rather than left axis deviation, making D the definitively correct diagnosis.
}

